\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl188\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Jesus, Thy far-extended fame
\par \pard\li225\sl188\slmult0 My drooping soul exalts to hear;
\par Thy name, Thy all-restoring name,
\par Is music in a sinner's ear.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl188\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Sinners of old Thou didst receive
\par \pard\li225\sl188\slmult0 With comfortable words and kind,
\par \pard\li225\sl188\slmult0\qj Their sorrows cheer, their wants relieve,
\par \pard\li225\sl188\slmult0 Heal the diseased, and cure the blind.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl188\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  And art Thou not the Saviour still\cf0 
\par \pard\li225\sl188\slmult0 In every place and age the same?
\par Has Thou forgot Thy gracious skill,
\par Or lost the virtue of Thy name?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl188\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4. Faith in Thy changeless name I have;
\par \pard\li225\sl188\slmult0 The good, The kind physician, Thou
\par Art able now our souls to save,
\par Art willing to restore them now.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl188\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Wouldst Thou the body's health restore,
\par \pard\li270\sl188\slmult0\qj And not regard the sin-sick soul?
\par The sin-sick soul Thou lov'st much more,
\par And surely Thou, shall make it whole.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl188\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. All my disease, my every sin,
\par \pard\li270\sl188\slmult0 To Thee, O Jesus, I confess;
\par In pardon, Lord, my cure begin,
\par \pard    And perfect it in holiness.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

